# WP3.4 D030 full-app host gesture fixture.
# Button ids: OCT-=0 OCT+=1 SEL=3 EDIT=6 SEQ=11 PLAY=12.
# Encoder ids: SELECT=0 KNOB1=2 KNOB2=3 KNOB3=4 KNOB4=5.
# Note masks are physical FM-1 key bits.

# Enter ordinary SEQ, select logical track 2 and page 2.
100 btn 11
200 keys 8
210 keys 0
300 btn 1

# SELECT motion before/beginning the hold must not leak into the new target.
350 enc 0 7
400 keys 16
400 enc 0 1

# Create two locks on T2 / global step 19: VOICE 254, FINE 126.
500 enc 2 -1
550 enc 3 -2

# Browse from FINE back to VOICE through the SELECT encoder.
600 enc 0 -1

# Same-poll EDIT down + SEL press must only arm; it may never delete.
700 btndown 6
700 btn 3

# Automatic screenshot at 1000 ms must still show the armed VOICE delete target.
# Any encoder movement while armed is drained/discarded.
900 enc 0 1
900 enc 2 -20

# Releasing EDIT cancels the arm and keeps both locks.
1100 btnup 6
1150 enc 0 1

# PLAY cancels a pending arm before toggling transport.
1300 btndown 6
1400 btn 12
1450 btnup 6

# Browse back to VOICE, arm it, then an extra physical key-down cancels the arm.
1550 enc 0 -1
1600 btndown 6
1700 keys 48
1750 keys 16
1800 btnup 6

# The lock still exists: SELECT +1 reaches FINE, -1 returns to VOICE.
1900 enc 0 1
1950 enc 0 -1

# Final valid delete: EDIT arms now, SEL confirms on a later poll.
2500 btndown 6
2600 btn 3
2650 btnup 6

# VOICE is now deleted exactly once; FINE remains selected internally.
# Automatic screenshot at 3000 ms must show DELETED K1 VOICE.
3100 keys 0
3300 end
